All source.b* blocks below are initial research and proposals from before Decision 14 was confirmed. Do not read them as current recommendations, preserved contracts, or approval requests. The turn budget model in movement.mjs and movement.test.mjs is also for historical comparison and is not a basis for the current time-based implementation. source.sha256 and proposal-source.md are frozen as initial provenance and must not be overwritten by this revision.

## Historical Record — Campaign Movement Numeric Review Proposal — #296

Status: proposal / NEW DESIGN v0.1 / awaiting explicit approval from @islee23520. Comparison against the original source pages is incomplete. Do not use as a product Core or data default. Existing characters, martial arts, equipment, lineages, and accepted rules are not changed.

### Historical Record — Sources and Scope of Verification

Request #296 requires explicit approval of values, units, and coefficients. Do not begin the #297 Core implementation before approval. Preserve source.b18–b26 on hero squads and concurrent progress. The fixed source.sha256 is 3bd57c0dbaee7da56e8bdbdf43889033a292d4874bbd9a747a771174c7d2d988.

The concepts of turn reach boundaries, stances, roads, multi-turn movement, and enemy ZOC were confirmed at [Total War Academy](https://academy.totalwar.com/campaign-moving-armies-exploration-and-stances/) (accessed 2026-09-28, HTML). It does not provide cost figures. Do not certify against the latest Warhammer III patch values, and do not copy naval transition rules to underground transfers.

[SJ Games Lite guide](https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/lite/) and [product 31-0004](https://warehouse23.com/products/gurps-lite-fourth-edition) confirm that it is a 32-page summary of the 4th edition. Because the Lite body PDF could not be obtained, the exact edition, printed/PDF page numbers, rounding, and original HP/FP rules are unverified. On the first page of the [official CharacterSheet.pdf](https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/resources/CharacterSheet.pdf), the ENCUMBRANCE/MOVE table confirms BL=ST²/5, the BL multipliers 1·2·3·6·10, and the Move multipliers 1·0.8·0.6·0.4·0.2. This is not a citation of the Lite body text. The index in the [Basic Set excerpt](https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/Basic/characters.pdf) is not a substitute source for the rule text or the Lite pages.

### Historical Record — Contracts to Preserve

Preserve the following: a maximum of 20 foot soldiers (heroes separate), a temporary foot-soldier squad leader when the commander is lost, the same command contract for AI, no priority by submission time or host, one world-time step per turn resolution, locking subsequent strategy commands only for squads taking part in combat, and splitting and merging only on the same node and floor. Movement, attack, interception, reinforcement, and stance are separate commands. A forced march cannot initiate an attack or interception but can be attacked, and camping cannot initiate an attack.

### Historical Record — Proposed Values and Integer Calculation

Do not convert one time step into hours, days, or km. The storage unit for abstract movement points (MP) is 1000u=1MP, with Q=1000. All coefficients and the way units are applied are new designs. basicMove is a non-negative integer from approved character input, and no default is created if it is missing. Do not automatically infer it from GURPS Basic Speed or apply CP adjustments.

personalU=floor(basicMove×1000×encPermille×healthPermille×fatiguePermille/1000³). squadBaseU is the minimum personalU among all actually walking members, including the commander, assigned heroes, and foot soldiers. turnBudgetU=floor(squadBaseU×stancePermille/1000). Round down only at the end, with no intermediate rounding down. Do not exclude members who cannot walk from the calculation, and do not put them on unapproved transport.

Load is summed per individual across equipment, weapons, armor, consumables, and assigned shared loads. It is compared in the same integer units as the approved BL, and if it equals a boundary, the lower tier applies. The limits are BL×[1,2,3,6,10], and the coefficients are [1000,800,600,400,200]. Anything over 10BL is rejected as OVER_CAPACITY. This proposal does not fix the rounding of the original BL.

Candidate state coefficients: health normal 1000 / walking-wounded 750 / unable to walk unaided 0; fatigue normal 1000 / fatigued 750 / exhausted 500 / unable to move 0. The thresholds for mapping HP and FP to these states, and the accumulation of recovery and fatigue, are unsupported before approval. These numbers are not GURPS facts.

Candidate stance coefficients: normal 1000, forced march 1500, ambush 500. Movement is rejected while garrison or camp is active. The movement stance is locked before the first move, and after moving only an ending stance is allowed. Releasing the ending stance does not resume movement or refill the budget within the same turn. Maintain usedForcedMarchThisTurn so that returning to normal does not clear the attack and interception restriction. This state transition must be approved and verified under a separate stance command contract.

### Historical Record — Edges, Reach, and Reservations

Candidate base edge costs (u): surface road 750, surface normal 1000, surface rough 1500, underground line 1000, explicitly specified entry/transfer 1250. edgeCostU=ceil(baseCostU×terrainPermille/1000)+surchargeU. Since base terrain is already reflected in the cost, apply additional adjustments only from explicitly approved inputs (test input 1000/0). The real-world length of a single edge is undecided, and the policy for splitting long segments or overriding costs is awaiting approval.

A surface edge must be on the same surface floor, and an underground edge on the same underground floor. Floor changes are allowed only for connection pairs specified on the map. Lack of a pass, a blockade, or a wrong floor is illegal rather than infinite cost. Every route is checked in the order adjacency → floor → pass → blockade → stance → ZOC → total cost, and within the same check stage the failure with the earlier route index is returned. Format, duplicate ID, and range errors are rejected before the route check. On failure, the position, budget, and composition remain unchanged, and no prefix is executed automatically.

Entering an enemy ZOC costs the normal amount and ends movement. Only an endpoint is allowed, and a command that exits past an intermediate ZOC is rejected entirely. Record stop=ZOC without converting the remaining accounting budget to 0. If the starting point is in a ZOC, a normal MOVE is not possible, and a separate retreat, attack, or permitted detour contract is needed. Reach is computed with a positive-cost Dijkstra, ZOC nodes are not expanded, and ties use the lexicographic order of the ASCII edgeId array. This search is outside the scope of the research calculator implementation.

A multi-turn reservation is a non-binding destination and intended route. Each turn the map, authority, enemies, and load are rechecked, and that turn''s command is confirmed separately. Do not automatically truncate and execute a command that exceeds the day''s budget. The remaining budget is not carried over, and if a single edge exceeds the turn budget, partial edge progress is not saved either.

### Historical Record — Hypothetical Squad Verification

These are not figures from real character cards. A is 1 commander (Basic Move 6, BL 20, load 15) and 8 foot soldiers (each Move 5, BL 20, load 30); B is 1 commander (Move 6, BL 45, load 40) and 12 foot soldiers (each Move 5, BL 20, load 50). At normal health and fatigue 1000, A has Normal 4000 / Forced March 6000 / Ambush 2000u, and B has Normal 3000 / Forced March 4500 / Ambush 1500u. If one B foot soldier is wounded at 750, that gives 2250u; if fatigue 750 is added on top, 1687u.

In the hypothetical map, S0→S1 is road 750, S1→S2 is road 750, S2→U0 is entrance 1250, U0→U1 is underground 1000, and U1→U2 is underground 1000. A''s Normal move pays 3750 to reach U1, leaving 250; B''s Normal move pays 2750 to reach U0, leaving 250. If B orders a move to U1, the whole order is rejected and B stays at S0 with 3000. A''s Forced March pays 4750 to reach U2, leaving 1250; B''s Forced March pays 3750 to reach U1, leaving 750.

If U1 is a ZOC, A''s Normal move keeps the remaining 250 and a stop marker after arriving at U1, and a Forced March order to U2 is rejected in full. Blocking an entrance edge also causes full rejection. On a route costing 4000, a budget of 4000 succeeds and 3999 fails. B''s multi-turn reservation can be expected to reach U0 on the first turn and U2 on the next, but the actual state is rechecked every turn.

### Historical Record — Determinism and Verification Scope

The offline packet uses arbitrary-precision BigInt multiplication and integer floor/ceil. External JSON numbers accept only safe non-negative integers, are rejected if they exceed the result limit, and are never clamped. Stable IDs are restricted to ASCII, and SHA-256 is applied to UTF-8 JSON with sorted object keys. Arrays that are semantically sets, such as map nodes/edges, squad members, and commands, are sorted by explicit ID, while the order of route arrays is preserved. Duplicate IDs are rejected before hashing. Costs, coefficients, inputs, and results go into the hash; submission time, host order, and translations do not. The packet hash is not the Core replay hash.

Simultaneous resolution must be validated against the same turn snapshot. Stable storage order must not be used as a priority for deciding the game winner. Valid-route conflicts, crossing movement, information/ambush, dynamic blockades, and combat context require a separately approved conflictRuleVersion. The cumulative cost/budget rational-number time model is only a candidate under review and is neither adopted nor implemented in this document. Retransmission receipts, command DAGs, conflict resolution, stance transitions, and authenticity verification of approval records are also not included in the completion claim of this single-MOVE calculator.

Verification packet location: movement.mjs and movement.test.mjs in the local research folder research/2026-09-28/tripothon/movement. It uses only Node''s built-in test/crypto modules. It runs two squads, road/underground/entrance, forced march, ZOC, blockade, boundary and 1u-short cases, malformed formats, duplicate IDs, overflow, immutability on rejection, and array-order-invariant hashing. This is research material separate from the GDD and is not released by a GDD PR alone.

### Historical Record — Decisions Remaining Before Approval

What remains: explicit approval record from @islee23520; the Lite source file/edition/exact page and rounding and HP/FP cross-check; units and all new coefficients; HP/FP state mapping; edge length policy; wounded transport; the readiness penalty for being hit during a forced march; stance change policy; ambush/scouting/dynamic collision; and the approved-data validator contract. Passing the draft''s coefficient check does not clear this gate. Distinguish between finishing a proposal for owner review and the full approval of #296.', '# 시간 기반 캠페인 이동 검토안 — 결정 14 / #296

현재 기준은 소유자 Intent 결정 14와 영웅 분대의 시간 기반 이동·이동 중 목표 교체·다섯 태세·AI 동일 계약이다. 대상별 사건 전이와 화면 분리, 역 없는 영지 계약을 함께 따른다. 아래 MOV-01~07 수치와 변환은 문서 병합과 별개로 소유자의 개별 승인을 기다리는 제안이다. 동시 전략 턴·턴 이동력은 현재 설계가 아니며, 판정은 독자 TRPG 핵심 규칙 체계를 따른다.

