## 15. Value Scales and Salvaged-Component Comparisons

### 15.1 Stellaris and Europa Universalis IV — Ethics Axes and Policy Slots [REF:VP-SLOTS]

- **[Comparison set]** For the 10 character value slots and the organization policy slots, the comparison set is Stellaris''s ethics pairs (Authority–Equality, Exclusivity–Openness, Militarism–Pacifism, Materialism–Spiritualism/Ritual) and policy slots, together with the Central, Innovation, and Diplomacy slots of Europa Universalis 4. Source texts for both games have not yet been collected.
- **Janseon**: Only the structure of axes and slots is compared. The original games'' galactic species names, ideology group names, and unique event text are not carried over.

### 15.2 Horizon Forbidden West — Salvaged-Component Economy [REF:HFW-SALVAGE]

- **[Document: Official Introduction]** The official PlayStation introduction (viewed 2026-09-12) explains that players craft weapons, equipment, and traps from parts salvaged from machines.
- **Janseon**: Only this economic tension is borrowed. Modules salvaged from beneath Seoul attach conditionally to equipment, traps, and weapons. They do not turn the basic unit class into archers, and the original''s proper nouns and crafting recipes are not brought over.', '> [!NOTE]

