INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, title_ko, summary, summary_ko, status, sort, source_path, body_md, body_ko_md) VALUES ('doc.Ui-Implementation-Pipeline', 'design', 'ui-implementation-pipeline', 'How UI Enters Code', 'UI가 코드로 들어오는 길', '', '', 'accepted', 41, 'Ui-Implementation-Pipeline.md', '# How UI Enters Code

Screens do not start in Unity. First the layout and stable names are fixed in an HTML mockup, and then the same contract is carried over to a uGUI Canvas.

## Short Path

1. Draw the screen in the mockup.
2. Fix the names and stages the player sees.
3. `UguiHudBuilder` creates the Canvas and `UiElementNames`.
4. EditMode checks names and structure, and PlayMode capture leaves a receipt.

Do not open an empty Canvas in Unity first and match the names afterward.

## Screens the Player Passes Through

| # | Screen | Stable Names |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | Title | `main-title-start` |
| 1 | Base Preparation | `stage-base-prep` |
| 2 | Expedition | `stage-expedition` |
| 3 | Encounter | `stage-encounter` |
| 4 | Resolution | `stage-resolution` |
| 5 | Formation | `formation-edit` |
| 6 | Combat | `battle-dock` |
| 7 | Settlement·Return | `settlement-panel` |



In the 12 target screens, number 10 is `Jeontu Baechi` (battle deployment) and number 11 is `Budae Jihwi` (unit command), and the actual document is placed in the unit command UI. The expedition can continue even after settlement, and return is one of the five endings.

Without changing information acquisition, trust, ledger projection, rooting, recruitment, death, or succession decisions, this only corrects the meaning of the combat phase where it conflicts with the combat authority added later (Decisions 11 and 13). This document revision requires no new Unity element names or runtime implementation.

The battlefield diagram in that draft is a blueprint explaining the spatial layout, not an actual game screen. Combat has no pause/resume and no slow-down/speed-up slots (owner decision, 2026-09-24). Orders are previewed and confirmed for squads before engagement, and a squad that has entered melee engagement receives no new orders. Retreat is a battle-wide order. There is no order queue slot.

World rules for the sortie phase continue in [Campaign](/gdd/rules/campaign-loop/), and runtime screen responsibilities continue in [Unity Architecture](/gdd/architecture/unity-architecture/).

## Example views

The screen grammar consists of objects within the world, not web panels. Owner lock, 2026-09-12. Mockups and frozen captures are in the repository.

| Panel | File |
| --- | --- |
| Moodboard, 11 panels | ui-layout-moodboard |
| Frozen capture | `GAME-REFERENCE/ui-layout-moodboard/images/frozen/` |
| Diegetic HUD | `GAME-REFERENCE/ui-ux-refs/images/diegetic-hud.png` |
| Combat and Formations | `GAME-REFERENCE/ui-ux-refs/images/battle.png`, `formation.png` |
