## 5.1 Time-Based Strategic Movement

Seoul fact: the time-based movement of Decision 14 (2026-09-28) replaces the simultaneous strategic turn goal. Squads move along legal routes while world time passes, and objectives, posture, stopping, and changes are independent commands. CampaignTurnDomain.cs:220-221 in the current implementation uses discrete turns, so it does not mean the target-movement model has shipped (https://github.com/islee23520/seoul-dengoku/blob/3e3c03349eafaaf88347d119a4bdd0c6d44abc53/GAME/Assets/Janseon/Core/CampaignTurnDomain.cs#L220-L221). Product authority: the strategic time cadence and speed conversion are not yet established.

## 5.2 The 334-Station Graph, Layers, and Transfers

Seoul fact: https://github.com/islee23520/seoul-dengoku/blob/3e3c03349eafaaf88347d119a4bdd0c6d44abc53/AGENTS.md#L61 distinguishes the 334-station movement graph, the three-station content of Area 1, and the 427-dong atlas. Surface adjacency is not a movement edge. Maintain the previously approved squad contract''s surface/underground layers, transfer and entrance nodes, and full-route legality checks. CK3 reference: depth-03-activities-travel-landless.md:273-375,475-482 covers the boundary between destination planning and the pathfinding engine, plus special adjacency data. Equating pathfinding algorithms with speed and cost is unproven.

## 5.3 Deterministic Encounters and Expedition Outcomes

Seoul fact: encounters in travel-and-encounters are reproduced from the seed, location, world time, noise, control, and squad state, and not every encounter is a battle. Return is not forced, and on-site outcomes are distinguished from entering CH6 battle. CK3 reference: the no-event probability inputs at depth-03-activities-travel-landless.md:319-346,516-527 differ from the effective probability of harmful events. Corrected static reference, limited to the PASS scope of depth-verification-20261027.md:1855-1900; actual firing frequency and loss rates are unverified.

## 5.4 Activities and Daily-Life Content

CK3 reference: the activity eligibility, invitations, arrival, phases, invalidation, and success rolls at depth-03-activities-travel-landless.md:124-174,180-271 are a structure in which location and companions bind the content. Do not port hunting and tournament calendars or pausing into Seoul. The monthly processing distribution at mechanics-01-time-and-pulse.md:183-210 is likewise only a cycle reference and not Seoul''s calendar. Product authority: activity types, phases, rewards, and frequency are not yet established.

## 5.5 Landless Play and Livelihood

CK3 reference: the camps, contracts, food, and entry/exit at depth-03-activities-travel-landless.md:376-437 are an example of a landless cycle. Maintain the correction at :23-77,516-541 that pam is not a landless camp identifier but the prefix of the relevant installed religion function. Seoul fact: the main body''s location, eligibility, and life execution follow SP-1.0.0. Product authority: whether to adopt landless camps, contract occupations, and food resources is itself not yet established. The alignment of WorldSeconds in EstateSimulation.cs:9-26,54-63 with the world Tick is unconfirmed.

