INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, title_ko, summary, summary_ko, status, sort, source_path, body_md, body_ko_md) VALUES ('doc.Archify-D04', 'system-design', 'archify-d04', 'D04 Achipai — Full Logic of Population, Labor, Employment, and Rations', 'D04 아치파이 — 인구·노동·고용·배급 전체 논리', '', '', 'accepted', 72, 'system-design/Archify-D04.md', '# D04 Achipai — Full Logic of Population, Labor, Employment, and Rations

This page shows, as structural diagrams, the machine inputs, validation order, contract calculations, state and conservation boundaries, and error and hold paths of the population, labor, employment, and ration domain. The sources are the relevant mechanism contract and the 2026-10-08 transition map; the approval status of numeric values follows the original contract.

## Machine Input and Validation Flow

```archify
{"domainId":"D04","diagramId":"d04-flow","moduleTitle":"D04 Operation Flow"}
```

Consumer contract (conservation-no-roll): Population identity partition conserved; sum(dt*availability*approvedTaskFactor), availability in [0,1], factor>=0; C factor table unresolved, never use A (a+2)/6.

## Calculation and Output

```text
population [bounded-symbolic-contract] N=|living cohort IDs|+|living individual IDs|; extract k: A-k,I+k; return r: A+r,I-r
summoned-subset [bounded-symbolic-contract] summoned IDs subset of individual IDs; summoning the already individualized three does not subtract three again
reservation [bounded-symbolic-contract] a.start < b.end AND b.start < a.end
remaining-demand [bounded-symbolic-contract] max(0,need-sum(distinct verified deliveries for same person,needId,unit))
wage-arrears [bounded-symbolic-contract] max(0,contractuallyDue-verifiedPaid)
D04-F1 [Candidate · Pre-approval] N=card(livingCohort)+card(livingIndividuals); extract k: cohort-k,individual+k; overlap=a.start<b.end && b.start<a.end
D04-F2 [Candidate · Pre-approval] effectiveHours=sum(dt*availability*taskFactor); A-only comparison factor=(a+2)/6; B/C require their own factor policy
D04-F3 [Candidate · Pre-approval] unmet=max(0,need-uniqueDelivered); arrears=max(0,due-paid)

```

The remaining contract leaves of D04 are preserved as a reference ledger linked to the operation flow. Historical reference formulas and unresolved values are not placed on operation edges.

## State Fields and Preservation Boundaries

- people — Person[] (existing member tokens linked to permanent PersonId)
- cohortId — string (existing cohort identifier)
- start,end — safe integer (same world-clock tick; scale not authored)
- need,delivered,wageDue,wagePaid — safe nonnegative integer (explicit identical contract item/currency unit)
- eligibility — authored source-bound requirement table (contract predicates)
- health — upstream approved state (upstream HP/FP and separate needs state)

The data owner is D04 design evidence only, and the maintained contracts are population, summoned-subset, reservation, remaining-demand, and wage-arrears. The state ownership boundaries are person token/cohort partition,living IDs,time reservations,actual work intervals,D02 availability,wage/ration receipts. Commit rules: Version-bound owner candidate; current grant/consent/receipt guards; preserve quantities/identities/consumed progress; atomic accepted receipt. Exact source contract referenced below.

## Error and Hold Codes

- Candidate errors: E_CONSERVATION, E_POLICY, E_UNIT, E_INPUT
- Existing evaluator errors: E_TYPE, E_DUPLICATE_ID, E_CHECKPOINT, E_RANGE, E_OVERLAP, E_VERSION, E_EVENT_CONFLICT, E_STALE_SNAPSHOT, E_GUARD, E_PROPOSAL_REQUIRED
- Adapter combination rules: tagged unresolved -> Held E_UNRESOLVED; malformed missing required key -> Rejected E_INPUT; stale -> E_REVISION; unit -> E_UNIT; conservation -> E_CONSERVATION. Authority/consent/feasibility privately distinct.

## Removal of Borrowed Formulas and Scope of Application

Borrowed formulas to remove: —. No confirmed GURPS arithmetic in inspected formulaSheet/evaluator; retain ordinary counts, sets, sums and policy locks. D09 reference explicitly invokes no contest.

This domain has no recorded new-module application entries yet.

Current scope limits: No domain-specific new original-trpg module. Reuse existing original bounded contracts; do not mark everything undecided. The next implementation unit is U-D04-population-labor-reconciliation(TOOL/tools/mechanisms/original-trpg/population-labor-reconciliation.mjs, TOOL/tools/mechanisms/original-trpg/population-labor-reconciliation.test.mjs). Separately from the approval of character and world values, this Achipai shows only the contract structure.

## Processing by Flow Node and Original Steps

- Population and reservation request — receives the checkpoint, exact event, revision, rules, and existing tokens/IDs. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[0])
- Format and unit check — safe non-negative integers and exact records. No numeric coercion or clamping. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[0]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[1])
- Token and person partition check — token/PersonId one-to-one and unique. Living is cohort/individual; dead is none. Existing aggregate and role references are valid. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[2])
- All role interval check — no positive [start,end) overlap for the same person. a.start<b.end AND b.start<a.end. Touching end/start is non-overlapping. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[3])
- Rule and request replay comparison — after the full state check, rules match; the same event plus full request is replayed, and any change is rejected. A new request uses the current revision. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[3]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[4])
- Replay of previous checkpoint — no additional population, reservation, or ration changes applied. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[3])
- Extraction, return, and reservation branch — uses only the same permanent IDs. Actual qualification, authority, and consent are separate policies. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[5])
- Aggregate-to-individual transfer — extracting k people is A-k,I+k; token, PersonId, original cohort, life, and name are preserved. Summoning is an individual subset, so population is not reduced again. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[4])
- Individual-to-original-aggregate return — returns the same ID to its original cohort. If a reservation remains, the release policy is unresolved and held. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[4])
- Living individual and existing role reservation — requires a living individual, an existing role, a positive interval, and a source qualification table. A single eligible boolean does not issue actual qualification. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[5])
- Full candidate invariant check — rechecks population total, identity, name, living frame, and shared time reservations. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[7])
- Checkpoint and receipt commit — commits one revision and an immutable event receipt. Issues no new persons, wages, or ration amounts. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[7])
- Qualification and release policy unresolved — holds only unresolved transitions such as actual qualification, return, and reservation release. Existing state is preserved. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- ID, overlap, and revision rejection — rejects malformed input, duplicate IDs, illegal locators, dead roles, overlaps, stale snapshots, changed events, and frame mismatches. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[0]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[3]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[7]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Actual ration record — verified fulfillment events and required amount for the same personId, needId, and unit. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Ration attribution and duplicate check — an identical record for the same event counts once. Differing content is a conflict. Stock and reservations are not rations. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Remaining purchase requirement — max(0,need-sum(distinct verified deliveries)). Food, water, and currency are not mixed. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Verified fulfillment and remaining demand — outputs only the actual delivered amount and the remaining purchase demand. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Same-currency obligation and payment — the approved contract''s due and the verified paid. The obligation cycle and wage amount, if undetermined, are held. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Arrears reconciliation — max(0,contractuallyDue-verifiedPaid). No new payment obligation is created. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Arrears reference — computes only the balance in the same currency and does not merge it with other individuals or contracts. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- ID, overlap, and revision rejection — rejects malformed input, duplicate IDs, illegal locators, dead roles, overlaps, stale snapshots, changed events, and frame mismatches. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[0]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[3]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[7]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Qualification and release policy unresolved — holds only unresolved transitions such as actual qualification, return, and reservation release. Existing state is preserved. (Source: d04.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d04.b9.orderedSteps[6])

