INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, title_ko, summary, summary_ko, status, sort, source_path, body_md, body_ko_md) VALUES ('doc.Archify-D17', 'system-design', 'archify-d17', 'D17 Archpie — Complete Logic of Negotiation, Trade, Peace, and Contracts', 'D17 아치파이 — 협상·거래·강화·계약 전체 논리', '', '', 'accepted', 85, 'system-design/Archify-D17.md', '# D17 Archpie — Complete Logic of Negotiation, Trade, Peace, and Contracts

This page shows, as a structural diagram, the machine inputs, validation order, contract calculations, state and conservation boundaries, and error and hold paths of the negotiation, trade, peace, and contract domain. The sources are the relevant mechanism contracts and the 2026-10-08 transition map; the approval status of numeric values follows the source contract.

## Machine Input and Validation Flow

```archify
{"domainId":"D17","diagramId":"d17-flow","moduleTitle":"D17 Operation Flow"}
```

Consumer contract (authority-and-conservation-with-optional-dialogue-contest): Same-unit demand minus offer, separate assent by required parties, repricing requires new acceptance; delivered+remaining conserved. Dialogue win may improve conveyed proposal evidence only, not assent.

## Calculation and Output

```text
demandSum [] sum(term.price.amount for eligible demand terms)
offerSum [] sum(term.price.amount for eligible offer terms)
proposalValue [] V=demandSum-offerSum
quantityConservation [] delivered_after + remaining_after = delivered_before + remaining_before for each signed term unless a separately supplied lawful quantity-changing event exists
revision [] accepted new event: ledger version +1; duplicate/reject: unchanged
D17-F1 [Candidate · Pre-approval] value=sum(eligible demand prices)-sum(eligible offer prices); value<=warScore never implies acceptance; deliveredAfter+remainingAfter=deliveredBefore+remainingBefore unless separately lawful quantity-changing event
D17-F2 [Candidate · Pre-approval] utility=sum(w_j*u_j(knownSnapshot)); registeredResponsePolicy may propose response; explicit required party consent/signature remains separate; no raw values-cast weight reuse

```

The remaining contract leaves of D17 are preserved as a reference ledger linked to the operation flow. Historical reference formulas and undetermined values are not placed on operation edges.

## State Fields and Preservation Boundaries

- version — safe nonnegative integer (ledger revision)
- war — WarSnapshot (war ID/score/casus-belli/endpoint status)
- proposal — Proposal | null (stable proposal ID and revision)
- terms — Term[] (one demand or offer per stable term ID)
- rights — RightSnapshot[] (stable right/asset/person/obligation ID)
- contracts — DeliveryContract[] (signed term obligation)
- history — event ID -> payload digest and receipt (event identity)

The data owner is the D17 negotiation and settlement ledger, and the maintained contracts are demandSum·offerSum·proposalValue·quantityConservation·revision. The state ownership boundary is terms and same-unit prices,proposal revision/snapshot,signers/fresh acceptances,reservations,contract delivered/remaining,cancellation/expiry/death evidence. Commit rule: Version-bound owner candidate; current grant/consent/receipt guards; preserve quantities/identities/consumed progress; atomic accepted receipt. Exact source contract referenced below.

## Error and Hold Codes

- Candidate errors: E_POLICY, E_AUTHORITY, E_CONSENT, E_REVISION, E_CONSERVATION
- Existing evaluator errors: E_TYPE, E_SCHEMA, E_VERSION, E_ID, E_CONSERVATION, E_PLEDGE, E_AUTHORITY, E_RIGHT, E_CONSENT, E_FEASIBILITY
- Adapter combination rules: tagged unresolved -> Held E_UNRESOLVED; malformed missing required key -> Rejected E_INPUT; stale -> E_REVISION; unit -> E_UNIT; conservation -> E_CONSERVATION. Authority/consent/feasibility privately distinct.

## Removal of Borrowed Formulas and Scope of Application

Borrowed formulas to remove: —. No confirmed GURPS arithmetic in inspected formulaSheet/evaluator; retain ordinary counts, sets, sums and policy locks. D09 reference explicitly invokes no contest.

- pure safe integer margin/outcome and caller-authorized projection, no profile/rating/receipt authority
- caller-supplied trusted boolean gates only; no provenance/authentication/world resolver, absent tag unsupported

Current scope limit: Named helper only; no complete authoritative domain state owner/transaction/consumer workbook. The next implementation unit is U-D17-proposal-assent-delivery(TOOL/tools/mechanisms/original-trpg/proposal-assent-delivery.mjs, TOOL/tools/mechanisms/original-trpg/proposal-assent-delivery.test.mjs). Separate from the approval of character and world values, this archpie shows only the contract structure.

## Processing by Flow Node and Original Steps

- Negotiable Boundary — [Per-Term Negotiation Eligibility] If D16 supplies &#124;W&#124;=100 before signing, the open proposal is discarded and only the fixed CB termination applies. New simultaneous-event priority is a D18 input. (Source: d17.b11.mechanisms[4].al​gorithm)
- Party and Term Conditions — [Per-Term Negotiation Eligibility] Signing authority and disposal authority are checked separately, and the term ID, demand/offer, beneficiary, scope of enforcement, third-party rights, required consent, feasibility, and duplicate collateral are all verified. (Source: d17.b11.mechanisms[0].al​gorithm)
- Registered Price and Same Unit — [Per-Term Negotiation Eligibility] Every term must have a registered price bound to the current proposal snapshot and revision. A missing price is not 0; it is undetermined. (Source: d17.b11.mechanisms[1].al​gorithm)
- Demand Sum − Offer Sum — [Per-Term Negotiation Eligibility] Demand sum minus offer sum is calculated exactly in the same price unit. Heterogeneous units of goods quantities are not added together. (Source: d17.b9.formulaSheet[2].e​xpression; d17.b9.formulaSheet[2].u​nit; d17.b9.formulaSheet[2].n​ull; d17.b9.formulaSheet[2].c​lamp; d17.b9.formulaSheet[2].r​ounding; d17.b9.formulaSheet[2].r​ng)
- Explicit Response — [Accept, Reject, Counterproposal] An authorized party''s acceptance is bound to the proposal revision and snapshot digest. Rejection and counterproposal are separate branches, and acceptance is never created from V<=W, favorability, trust, or a dialogue win. (Source: d17.b11.mechanisms[2].al​gorithm)
- Explicit Repricing — [Accept, Reject, Counterproposal] When relevant state changes, a new revision and snapshot are created under the same proposal identity, and all past acceptances are invalidated. (Source: d17.b11.mechanisms[3].al​gorithm)
- New Acceptance and Term Recheck — [Accept, Reject, Counterproposal] The new price, authority, third-party rights, consent, feasibility, and reservations are rechecked at acceptance/signing, and a new receipt is required. The existing reference evaluator does not recheck terms immediately upon repricing, so that difference is left unverified. (Source: domain contract flow and detailed term references)
- Recheck at Signing — [Single Signing, Split Performance] Authority, term eligibility, price, and exclusive reservations are checked again against the currently valid acceptance snapshot. (Source: d17.b9.commitPoint)
- One Settlement ID — [Single Signing, Split Performance] Valid reservations are acquired atomically, and one settlement ID and per-clause delivery obligations are created. Goods and persons are never teleported or duplicated. (Source: d17.b11.mechanisms[5].al​gorithm)
- Partial Performance Conserved — [Single Signing, Split Performance] Delivered+remaining is conserved per clause, and only the quantity actually delivered moves to delivered. Cancellation, death, suspension, or breach does not reverse amounts already completed. (Source: d17.b9.formulaSheet[3].e​xpression; d17.b9.formulaSheet[3].u​nit; d17.b9.formulaSheet[3].n​ull; d17.b9.formulaSheet[3].c​lamp; d17.b9.formulaSheet[3].r​ounding; d17.b9.formulaSheet[3].r​ng)
- Recheck of Remaining Obligations — [Single Signing, Split Performance] Only the remaining obligations are rechecked against the current contract clauses. Remedies, deadlines, compensation, changes in trust, and termination effects are not issued if undetermined. (Source: d17.b11.mechanisms[6].al​gorithm)
- Authorized Cancellation — [Cancellation, Death, Expiry, Forgery] Cancelling an open proposal requires authority. Cancelling a signed contract follows the relevant clause, and completed deliveries are preserved. (Source: d17.b9.lifecycle.cancel)
- Recheck on Loss of Signer — [Cancellation, Death, Expiry, Forgery] Death or loss of authority invalidates the old acceptance and requires a per-contract recheck. Not all obligations are terminated at once. (Source: d17.b9.lifecycle.death)
- Expiry Only by Registered Deadline — [Cancellation, Death, Expiry, Forgery] Only an approved deadline or invalidation condition can expire a proposal. There is no default period. (Source: d17.b9.lifecycle.expiry)
