| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[0].chosenOpti​on | "A" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[0].applicatio​n | "Treaty indivisible clauses, legal-effect events, and physical-handoff events are distinct. Concrete CB, truce, reparation, captive, and superior-contract entries remain authored inputs rather than invented defaults." |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[1].row | "D12" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[1].decisionId​ | "T68-D17-PRICE-ACCEPTANC​E" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[1].chosenOpti​on | "A" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[1].applicatio​n | "Asset value, action cost, and actor-specific acceptance are separate. A missing registered price blocks final signature; V<=W is never automatic consent. Relevant state changes require explicit reevaluation on a new snapshot and invalidate old acceptance." |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[2].row | "D17" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[2].decisionId​ | "GP-07" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[2].chosenOpti​on | "B" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[2].applicatio​n | "Unassigned title and superior-contract records may be authored as proposals for item-by-item approval. The mechanism may validate supplied ratification records but cannot create holders, periods, or procedures." |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[3].row | "D19" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[3].decisionId​ | "T68-D11-CONTRACT-RECALL​" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[3].chosenOpti​on | "A" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[3].applicatio​n | "Each contract supplies authority, duration, duties, breach, ratification, expiry/death, conflict, and physical handoff clauses. No unconditional recall or automatic return is inferred." |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[4].row | "D22" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[4].decisionId​ | "T68-NUMERIC-DESIGN-ASSU​MPTIONS" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[4].chosenOpti​on | "B" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.sealed​Selections[4].applicatio​n | "Common units are explicit before formula coefficients. D17 accepts exact integer price-unit inputs only; coefficients and tables remain separately approved versioned inputs." |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.select​ionRule | "All 37 decision rows were read through their consequences. D06, D12, D17, D19, and D22 directly constrain D17. Every other row is recorded in proposals.json as deferred-with-trace rather than called irrelevant." |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.resear​chLimit | "Prior CK3/Norland D17 dossiers and the 2026-10-06 D17 proposal sheet are comparison evidence, not Seoul numeric authority. No external price, acceptance threshold, term duration, reservation priority, or breach coefficient is adopted." |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.gurpsL​ike.basis | "task-25-gurps-like-basi​s-20261008/basis.json" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.gurpsL​ike.workedChecks | "task-25-gurps-like-basi​s-20261008/worked-checks​.json" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.gurpsL​ike.D17NumericApplicabil​ity | "none" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.authority.gurpsL​ike.reason | "Negotiation consent and legal feasibility are not reaction rolls or quick contests. The public Lite reaction structure explicitly does not force contractual consent. D17 uses no 3d6, CP, skill, damage, or derived-character formula." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d17.b11.mechanisms[0].id​ | "ELIGIBILITY" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[0].ap​proved | true |
| Operation — Party and Item Conditions | d17.b11.mechanisms[0].al​gorithm | "Below the D16 endpoint, an authorized actor may submit itemized demands/offers. Finalization requires distinct signer/disposer authority, stable subject and beneficiary IDs, no unauthorized third-party right, explicit required consent, actual feasibility, and one pledge per subject within the proposal." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d17.b11.mechanisms[1].id​ | "VALUATION" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[1].ap​proved | true |
| Operation — Registered Price and Same Unit | d17.b11.mechanisms[1].al​gorithm | "Every final term carries a registered price record with version, snapshot digest, exact integer amount, and one common price unit. V=sum(demands)-sum(offer​s). Missing or stale price makes valuation unresolved and blocks acceptance/signature; it is never free." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d17.b11.mechanisms[2].id​ | "RESPONSE" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[2].ap​proved | true |
| Operation — Explicit Response | d17.b11.mechanisms[2].al​gorithm | "Acceptance is an explicit receipt by an authorized party bound to proposal revision and snapshot digest. Rejection and counteroffer are explicit branches. V<=W, positive reaction, high trust, or favorable relationship never creates consent." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d17.b11.mechanisms[3].id​ | "REPRICE" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[3].ap​proved | true |
| Operation — Explicit Repricing | d17.b11.mechanisms[3].al​gorithm | "A relevant state change preserves proposal identity only through an explicit reprice event that creates a new revision/snapshot, invalidates all old acceptance receipts, revalidates terms, and requires renewed acceptance before signature." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d17.b11.mechanisms[4].id​ | "ENDPOINT" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[4].ap​proved | true |
| Operation — Negotiable Boundary | d17.b11.mechanisms[4].al​gorithm | "If D16 supplies &#124;W&#124;=100 before signature, discard the open proposal and consume only the valid casus-belli endpoint result. Out-of-goal terms, third-party rights, and voluntary extras are not forced. Same-boundary priority remains D18 input rather than a D17 invention." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d17.b11.mechanisms[5].id​ | "SIGN" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[5].ap​proved | true |
| Operation — One Settlement ID | d17.b11.mechanisms[5].al​gorithm | "On a valid accepted snapshot, atomically verify and acquire supplied reservations, emit exactly one settlement ID, apply supplied legal effects, and create per-term delivery obligations. Signature does not teleport or duplicate property or people." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d17.b11.mechanisms[6].id​ | "DELIVERY" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[6].ap​proved | true |
| Operation — Recheck Remaining Obligations | d17.b11.mechanisms[6].al​gorithm | "Delivery advances exact delivered and remaining quantities under custody/route facts. Partial completion survives interruption, death, cancellation, and breach. Only remaining obligation is revalidated; remedy and timing require supplied contract clauses." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d17.b11.mechanisms[7].id​ | "IDEMPOTENCY" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[7].ap​proved | true |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d17.b11.mechanisms[7].al​gorithm | "A repeated event ID with the same canonical payload returns its stored receipt; a different payload under the same ID is rejected. A completed settlement/result ID is never applied twice." |
