| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d18.b11.sourceClaims[3].​rule | "Battle orders arrive immediately; the body squad leader may comply, partially comply or act independently. After actual execution results, appraisal belongs to the original issuing commander person and becomes that person’s memory and later assignment/trust evidence. Compliance and performance remain separate, with original sender, command and result identity preserved; subordinate autonomy does not transfer appraisal ownership." |
