### SEOUL-CARGO-CONSERVATION — Cargo Material Conservation

Status: Optional policy scope. Owner: D06/D13.

Formula: `parentAtoms=disjointUnion(child1,child2); qParent=q1+q2; root retired`. Input: same material units/atoms. Output unit: same material quantity.

Limits: Two separate children of the same material must cover the original without remainder. Fractional splitting, loss rates, ownership transfer, and receipt conventions are not specified.

- cargoSplit: Input `{"parent":["a","b","c","d","e"],"children":[["a","b"],["c","d","e"]]}` → Result `{"childQuantities":[2,3],"activeQuantity":5,"root":"retired"}`. The separated material of the children sums to the original, and the retired parent is not counted again in available stock.
- cargoDuplicate: Input `{"parent":["a","b","c"],"children":[["a","b"],["b","c"]]}` → Result `{"status":"invalid-input","value":null}`. The input violates the shape, range, or conservation conditions, so no result is produced.
- cargoOmitted: Input `{"parent":["a","b","c"],"children":[["a"],["b"]]}` → Result `{"status":"invalid-input","value":null}`. The input violates the shape, range, or conservation conditions, so no result is produced.
- cargoUnknown: Input `{"parent":null,"children":[["a"],["b"]]}` → Result `{"status":"unresolved","value":null}`. A required input or an applicable rule is missing, so the result remains unresolved.

### SEOUL-CUTOFF — Inclusive Cutoff

Owner: D06/D05. Formula: `temporalEligibility=verifiedArrival AND arrivalAt<=cutoff`.

Arrival ≤ cutoff only determines temporal eligibility for inclusion. Final available stock additionally requires separate identity, custody, and rights, as well as any applicable acceptance conditions. The two-party confirmation case in this document is an unadopted conditional proposal that adds confirmation by the current custodian. Arrival at the same moment does not bypass this.

- cutEqual: Input `{"arrival":600,"cutoff":600,"verified":true}` → Result `{"temporalEligibility":true,"finalAvailableStock":null}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions defined above and does not imply any additional policy.
- cutBefore: Input `{"arrival":599,"cutoff":600,"verified":true}` → Result `{"temporalEligibility":true,"finalAvailableStock":null}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions defined above and does not imply any additional policy.
- cutLate: Input `{"arrival":601,"cutoff":600,"verified":true}` → Result `{"stillExists":true,"temporalEligibility":false,"finalAvailableStock":null}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions defined above and does not imply any additional policy.
- cutFailed: Input `{"arrival":600,"cutoff":600,"verified":false}` → Result `{"temporalEligibility":false,"finalAvailableStock":null}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions defined above and does not imply any additional policy.
- cutUnknown: Input `{"arrival":600,"cutoff":600,"verified":null}` → Result `{"status":"unresolved","value":null}`. Unresolved policies or premises are not replaced with 0, prohibition, or success.
- cutEqualMissingCustodian: Input `{"arrival":600,"cutoff":600,"verified":true,"currentCustodianConfirmed":false,"receiverConfirmed":true,"identityCustodyRightsValid":true}` → Result `{"temporalEligibility":true,"receiptComplete":false,"finalAvailableStock":false}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions defined above and does not imply any additional policy.

### SEOUL-RELATION-CLASS — Directed Trust Classification

Status: Seoul-approved scope. Owner: D07.

Formula: `friend=T>=25;enemy=T<=-25;nemesis=T<=-50`. Input: directed known T[A,B]. Output unit: three independent booleans.

Limits: Directed trust must be known. Enemy and nemesis can both be true at once, and no exclusive display priority is created. Increase/decrease, decay, symmetry, and authority are separate.

- trust24: Input `{"T":24}` → Result `{"friend":false,"enemy":false,"nemesis":false}`. Each inclusive threshold was compared independently. This is not a trust change or a new authority.
- trust25: Input `{"T":25}` → Result `{"friend":true,"enemy":false,"nemesis":false}`. Each inclusive threshold was compared independently. This is not a trust change or a new authority.
- trust-24: Input `{"T":-24}` → Result `{"friend":false,"enemy":false,"nemesis":false}`. Each inclusive threshold was compared independently. This is not a trust change or a new authority.
- trust-25: Input `{"T":-25}` → Result `{"friend":false,"enemy":true,"nemesis":false}`. Each inclusive threshold was compared independently. This is not a trust change or a new authority.
- trust-49: Input `{"T":-49}` → Result `{"friend":false,"enemy":true,"nemesis":false}`. Each inclusive threshold was compared independently. This is not a trust change or a new authority.
- trust-50: Input `{"T":-50}` → Result `{"friend":false,"enemy":true,"nemesis":true}`. Each inclusive threshold was compared independently. This is not a trust change or a new authority.
- trustUnknown: Input `{"T":null}` → Result `{"status":"unresolved","value":null}`. A required input or an applicable rule is missing, so the result remains unresolved.

### SEOUL-NEGOTIATION-V — Negotiation Demand and Offer Value

Status: Seoul-approved scope. Owner: D17.

Formula: `V=sum(demandPrices)-sum(offerPrices)`. Input: registered same-snapshot prices. Output unit: price-score, not W/money.

Limits: All prices must be registered under the same war, proposal version, and snapshot. Unregistered prices and the acceptance coefficient are unresolved, and V<=W is not automatic acceptance.

- vKnown: Input `{"demands":[17,8],"offers":[6],"registered":true,"sameSnapshot":true}` → Result `{"V":19,"acceptance":null}`. The offer sum was subtracted from the registered demand sum. A known 0 differs from an unresolved unregistered value, and acceptance is separate.
- vZero: Input `{"demands":[17],"offers":[17],"registered":true,"sameSnapshot":true}` → Result `{"V":0,"acceptance":null}`. The offer sum was subtracted from the registered demand sum. A known 0 differs from an unresolved unregistered value, and acceptance is separate.
- vUnknown: Input `{"demands":[17,null],"offers":[6],"registered":false,"sameSnapshot":true}` → Result `{"status":"unresolved","value":null,"signatureBlocked":true}`. A required input or an applicable rule is missing, so the result remains unresolved.
- vStale: Input `{"demands":[17,8],"offers":[6],"registered":true,"sameSnapshot":false}` → Result `{"status":"invalid-input","value":null}`. The input violates the shape, range, or conservation conditions, so no result is produced.

### SEOUL-W-ENDPOINT — War Score Endpoints

Status: Seoul-approved scope. Owner: D16/D17.

Formula: `valid cause and beneficiary: abs(W)<100 negotiation eligible; W=100 force victory; W=-100 force defeat`. Input: known W in -100..100, cause/beneficiary facts. Output unit: symbolic mode.

Limits: W must be a known value from −100 to 100. Validity of the casus belli and beneficiary is checked first. Composition, cap adjustment, prices, acceptance, and simultaneous priority are not newly defined.

- w99: Input `{"W":99,"cause":true,"beneficiary":true}` → Result `{"mode":"negotiation-eligible","acceptance":null}`. Validity was checked first, and then exact endpoints were distinguished from the interior range.
- w100: Input `{"W":100,"cause":true,"beneficiary":true}` → Result `{"mode":"force-victory"}`. Validity was checked first, and then exact endpoints were distinguished from the interior range.
- wMinus100: Input `{"W":-100,"cause":true,"beneficiary":true}` → Result `{"mode":"force-defeat"}`. Validity was checked first, and then exact endpoints were distinguished from the interior range.
- wInvalidCause: Input `{"W":100,"cause":false,"beneficiary":true}` → Result `{"mode":"invalidity-first","endpointEffect":null}`. Validity was checked first, and then exact endpoints were distinguished from the interior range.
- wOutside: Input `{"W":101,"cause":true,"beneficiary":true}` → Result `{"status":"invalid-input","value":null}`. The input violates the shape, range, or conservation conditions, so no result is produced.
- wUnknown: input `{"W":null,"cause":true,"beneficiary":true}` → result `{"status":"unresolved","value":null}`. Because a required input or an applicable rule is missing, the result is kept undetermined.

### SEOUL-SINGLE-RESULT — Single Closure and Result ID

Owner: D18/D17. Formula: `Any ResultId is applied at most once; settlementCount changes only for an actual valid war-closure result under current authority/order/version; other results do not close the war`.

A new ResultId by itself is not grounds for closing a war. The closure settlement count changes only when the result is an actual valid war-closure result and authority, version, and event order are all in place. An ordinary result does not close the war even if it is applied once.

- resultNew: input `{"id":"R-a","applied":[],"closed":false,"validBoundary":true,"actualValidWarClosureResult":true,"priorSettlementCount":0}` → result `{"effect":"apply-once","settlementCount":1}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions qualified above and does not imply any additional policy.
- resultRepeat: input `{"id":"R-a","applied":["R-a"],"closed":true,"validBoundary":true,"actualValidWarClosureResult":true,"priorSettlementCount":1}` → result `{"effect":"no-new-effect","settlementCount":1}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions qualified above and does not imply any additional policy.
- resultClosed: input `{"id":"R-b","applied":["R-a"],"closed":true,"validBoundary":true,"actualValidWarClosureResult":true,"priorSettlementCount":1}` → result `{"effect":"no-new-effect","settlementCount":1}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions qualified above and does not imply any additional policy.
- resultUnknown: input `{"id":"R-a","applied":[],"closed":false,"validBoundary":null,"actualValidWarClosureResult":true,"priorSettlementCount":0}` → result `{"status":"unresolved","value":null}`. An undecided policy or premise is not replaced with 0, prohibition, or success.
- resultNonClosure: input `{"id":"R-note","applied":[],"closed":false,"validBoundary":true,"actualValidWarClosureResult":false,"priorSettlementCount":0}` → result `{"effect":"apply-once-nonclosure","settlementCount":0,"warClosed":false}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions qualified above and does not imply any additional policy.

The encumbrance rows are BL multiplier 1/2/3/6/10, move factor 1/0.8/0.6/0.4/0.2, and dodge modifier 0/−1/−2/−3/−4. Which row the actual load belongs to, as well as the specific rounding and minimum movement, is not determined by this preview alone. The base values of basic speed, move, and dodge are also not back-calculated.

The abbreviated range table, in yd, is 2:0, 3:-1, 5:-2, 7:-3, 10:-4, 15:-5, 20:-6, 30:-7, 50:-8, 70:-9, 100:-10, 150:-11, 200:-12, 300:-13, 500:-14, 700:-15. Only the first row explicitly covers 2 yd or less. Row selection for intermediate ranges and values beyond 700 yd require the full table rules. Hit locations are torso 0, arm/leg −2, groin −3, hand −4, face −5, skull −7, and the vital-spot −3 and eye −9 for Imp/Pi attacks are conditional notations. These values are not used to create protection locations or injury multipliers.

The exceptions of the relevant rules take precedence over general cost round-up and action/combat round-down. When the specific exceptions for BL or actual movement are unknown, do not apply the general convention to produce a definite result. The 3d comparison in the introduction is not a complete success/failure classification, so do not add critical results from extreme dice.

Population conservation applies only to representational movement without birth, death, migration, or capture. The reservation-boundary allowance only determines positive-interval occupancy by the same person; the zero-time action policy is undecided, and equipment/facility capacity is not guaranteed. Deadline inclusion determines only temporal eligibility; final available stock separately requires handover, identity, custody, and rights conditions. Two-party confirmation is computed as an unadopted conditional proposal. Trust −50 satisfies both the enemy and nemesis conditions and does not newly set an exclusive display priority. V and W are separate numbers, and an unregistered price is not free. A valid cause and beneficiary are checked first, then ±100 is processed; no undecided same-time event-type priority is invented to decide a winner.

### SEOUL-CARGO-RECEIPT-GUARDS — Proposed Two-Party Confirmation for Cargo Receipt (Not Adopted)

Unadopted conditional proposal. Owner: D06/D13. Formula: `receiptComplete=currentCustodianConfirmed AND receiverConfirmed; finalAvailable requires temporal eligibility AND receiptComplete AND identity/custody/rights AND all other applicable receipt conditions`.

Additional custodian confirmation is an unadopted proposal. The following cases are an unadopted conditional model that assumes both confirmation by the current custodian AND confirmation by the receiver are required. The actual selection data directly supports only the receiver''s confirmation signature. Nor is this weakened into a rule that receiver confirmation alone makes the final stock available. Identity, custody, and rights conditions and the authentication protocol remain separate.

- Unadopted two-party confirmation proposal case. receipt-false-false: input `{"currentCustodianConfirmed":false,"receiverConfirmed":false,"temporalEligibility":true,"identityCustodyRightsValid":true,"otherReceiptConditions":true}` → result `{"receiptComplete":false,"finalAvailableStock":false}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions qualified above and does not imply any additional policy.
- Unadopted two-party confirmation proposal case. receipt-false-true: input `{"currentCustodianConfirmed":false,"receiverConfirmed":true,"temporalEligibility":true,"identityCustodyRightsValid":true,"otherReceiptConditions":true}` → result `{"receiptComplete":false,"finalAvailableStock":false}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions qualified above and does not imply any additional policy.
- Unadopted two-party confirmation proposal case. receipt-true-false: input `{"currentCustodianConfirmed":true,"receiverConfirmed":false,"temporalEligibility":true,"identityCustodyRightsValid":true,"otherReceiptConditions":true}` → result `{"receiptComplete":false,"finalAvailableStock":false}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions qualified above and does not imply any additional policy.
- Unadopted two-party confirmation proposal case. receipt-true-true: input `{"currentCustodianConfirmed":true,"receiverConfirmed":true,"temporalEligibility":true,"identityCustodyRightsValid":true,"otherReceiptConditions":true}` → result `{"receiptComplete":true,"finalAvailableStock":true}`. This result is a calculation under the formula and state conditions qualified above and does not imply any additional policy.
- Unadopted two-party confirmation proposal case. receipt-rights-missing: input `{"currentCustodianConfirmed":true,"receiverConfirmed":true,"temporalEligibility":true,"identityCustodyRightsValid":null,"otherReceiptConditions":true}` → result `{"receiptComplete":true,"finalAvailableStock":null,"status":"unresolved"}`. An undecided policy or premise is not replaced with 0, prohibition, or success.

