INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, title_ko, summary, summary_ko, status, sort, source_path, body_md, body_ko_md) VALUES ('doc.Mechanism-D04', 'system-design', 'mechanism-d04', 'D04 Population, Labor, Employment, and Rationing Operating Contract and Official Sheet', 'D04 인구·노동·고용·배급 작동 계약과 공식 시트', '', '', 'accepted', 93, 'system-design/Mechanism-D04.md', '# D04 Population, Labor, Employment, and Rationing Operating Contract and Official Sheet

## Game Logic Overhaul Alignment Boundary

This document retains its existing proposal status. The formulas, tables, and blueprints are neither implementation facts of Seoul nor approved figures. The Seoul-fact / CK3-reference / product-authority distinctions in the linked chapters below and SP-1.0.0 take precedence, and undecided values are not interpreted as 0 or any arbitrary default. The deep-survey discrepancy totals and clan formulas are not adopted.

[Corresponding Chapters and Confirmed Grounds](/gdd/rules/economy-and-logistics/)

Personalizing and reverting aggregate population only changes how existing tokens and permanent IDs are represented. Time-interval reservations and actual rations for the same person are checked in a single ledger so that labor and quantities are conserved. Employment eligibility, wages, ration amounts, cycles, and health-to-productivity conversion are deferred.

Status: a scoped operating contract. It distinguishes the public Lite''s reference calculations, Seoul''s approved procedures and preservation rules, and unapproved proposals. A proposal-held item is a deferred entry that cannot be executed, and it is neither 0 nor an approved figure. This document does not imply full-domain numerical completion or a runtime implementation.

[Domain Design](/gdd/system-design/mechanism-design-index-d04/) · [Character Sheet and Calculations](/gdd/system-design/character-sheet-formulas/) · [Saving and Versions](/gdd/rules/save-and-determinism/) · [Singleplayer Contract](/gdd/system-design/singleplayer-design-sp-1-0-0/)

## Processing Order and Responsibility Boundaries

1. Validate the complete checkpoint and units, and confirm the one-to-one correspondence between tokens and permanent IDs as well as the partitioning of the surviving population.
2. Check for positive-length time-interval overlaps for the same person across all roles.
3. Compare the full event content and version to distinguish an exact retransmission from a changed duplicate.
4. Personalization and reversion keep the same tokens and IDs. Actual eligibility for a role reservation is a separate approval input.
5. Only actual rations for the same person, demand, and unit are deduplicated and then subtracted from the remaining demand.
6. After confirming that population, identity, and reservations are preserved in the candidate state, apply it with a single checkpoint and receipt.

## Normalized Data and Formula Contract

Declare together the owner, read/write scope, units, snapshot, and point of application. Validation of formats and conservation formulas does not substitute for actual ledger issuance or the adoption of undecided functions. rulesVersion and the hash of the linked canonical source identify the source version and do not create any arbitrary new execution version.

