INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, title_ko, summary, summary_ko, status, sort, source_path, body_md, body_ko_md) VALUES ('doc.Mechanism-D05', 'system-design', 'mechanism-d05', 'D05 Production, Construction, Storage, and Repair Operating Contract and Official Sheet', 'D05 생산·건설·보관·수리 작동 계약과 공식 시트', '', '', 'accepted', 94, 'system-design/Mechanism-D05.md', '# D05 Production, Construction, Storage, and Repair Operating Contract and Official Sheet

## Game Logic Overhaul Alignment Boundary

This document retains its existing proposal status. The formulas, tables, and blueprints are neither implementation facts of Seoul nor approved figures. The Seoul-fact / CK3-reference / product-authority distinctions in the linked chapters below and SP-1.0.0 take precedence, and undecided values are not interpreted as 0 or any arbitrary default. The deep-survey discrepancy totals and clan formulas are not adopted.

[Corresponding Chapters and Confirmed Grounds](/gdd/rules/economy-and-logistics/)

Separate verified arrivals, actual inventory, required-demand reservations, approved jobs, and per-stage consumption. On interruption, preserve fractional progress and both consumed and unused physical goods. Before entering the output or storage stage, a storage reservation must be secured at the relevant destination; per-recipe yield, speed, and recovery amounts are deferred.

Status: a scoped operating contract. It distinguishes the public Lite''s reference calculations, Seoul''s approved procedures and preservation rules, and unapproved proposals. A proposal-held item is a deferred entry that cannot be executed, and it is neither 0 nor an approved figure. This document does not imply full-domain numerical completion or a runtime implementation.

[Domain Design](/gdd/system-design/mechanism-design-index-d05/) · [Personal Sheet and Calculations](/gdd/system-design/character-sheet-formulas/) · [Save and Versioning](/gdd/rules/save-and-determinism/) · [Singleplayer Contract](/gdd/system-design/singleplayer-design-sp-1-0-0/)

## Processing Order and Responsibility Boundaries

1. Check identity, rules, revisions, and existing result IDs, and reject omissions and conflicts before writing.
2. Approved body states are read-only, and duplicate labor loss from the same body revision or effect is prevented.
3. At the same timestamp, verify arrivals first, then reserve required consumption, contracts, and supplies from actual inventory.
4. Only approved jobs proceed, and only when all per-recipe workforce, input, power, facility, and storage conditions are satisfied.
5. Apply consumption only once and preserve the exact fractional progress.
6. If there is no output or storage reservation, wait at the previous completed stage. Securing a reservation alone does not complete settlement of the output.
7. After the preservation check, atomically apply the result together with the effect settlement key and revision.

## Normalized Data and Formula Contract

Declare together the owner, read/write scope, units, snapshot, and point of application. Validation of formats and conservation formulas does not substitute for actual ledger issuance or the adoption of undecided functions. rulesVersion and the hash of the linked canonical source identify the source version and do not create any arbitrary new execution version.

