INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, title_ko, summary, summary_ko, status, sort, source_path, body_md, body_ko_md) VALUES ('doc.Mechanism-D06', 'system-design', 'mechanism-d06', 'D06 Movement, Cargo, Map, and Observation Operating Contract and Official Sheets', 'D06 이동·화물·지도·관측 작동 계약과 공식 시트', '', '', 'accepted', 95, 'system-design/Mechanism-D06.md', '# D06 Movement, Cargo, Map, and Observation Operating Contract and Official Sheets

## Game Logic Overhaul Alignment Boundary

This document retains its existing proposal status. The formulas, tables, and blueprints are neither implementation facts of Seoul nor approved figures. The Seoul-fact / CK3-reference / product-authority distinctions in the linked chapters below and SP-1.0.0 take precedence, and undecided values are not interpreted as 0 or any arbitrary default. The deep-survey discrepancy totals and clan formulas are not adopted.

[Corresponding Chapters and Confirmed Grounds](/gdd/rules/travel-activities-and-landless/)

Units move only along segments whose actual connection, passage rights, and passability have all been verified. Remaining movement distance and the material identity of cargo are preserved, and observed knowledge is kept separate from current world facts. Units that have actually arrived may join a battle in progress, but do not retroactively join a battle that has already ended.

Status: a scoped operating contract. It distinguishes the public Lite''s reference calculations, Seoul''s approved procedures and preservation rules, and unapproved proposals. A proposal-held item is a deferred entry that cannot be executed, and it is neither 0 nor an approved figure. This document does not imply full-domain numerical completion or a runtime implementation.

[Domain Design](/gdd/system-design/mechanism-design-index-d06/) · [Character Sheets and Calculations](/gdd/system-design/character-sheet-formulas/) · [Saves and Versions](/gdd/rules/save-and-determinism/) · [Singleplayer Contract](/gdd/system-design/singleplayer-design-sp-1-0-0/)

## Processing Order and Responsibility Boundaries

1. Reads the identities of routes, movers, cargo, observations, time, rules, and snapshots, and rejects duplicates, unit mismatches, and version conflicts.
2. Verifies the actual connection, passage rights, and segment passability. Unverified status is never replaced with allowed or false.
3. Separates individual Move and load reference calculations from Seoul''s strategic movement speed. Only the approved movement amount is subtracted from the remaining distance.
4. When blocked, keeps the completed distance and replans. A cargo split retires the parent only when the disjoint union of the child atoms equals the parent.
5. Verifies arrival first, then compares it against the deadline to check that it is at or before it. Final available stock separately requires recipient confirmation and applicable rights and storage checks.
6. A report updates only the observer''s knowledge, which carries a source, an observation time, and a reference time.
7. Reflects actual arrivals joining a battle in progress, and records a result or revision that passes all checks exactly once.

## Normalized Data and Formula Contract

Declare together the owner, read/write scope, units, snapshot, and point of application. Validation of formats and conservation formulas does not substitute for actual ledger issuance or the adoption of undecided functions. rulesVersion and the hash of the linked canonical source identify the source version and do not create any arbitrary new execution version.

