      "source": "sp1.b49"
    },
    {
      "id": "arrival-inclusion-at-cutoff",
      "statement": "verified arrival at or before the consumption cutoff enters that cutoff''s destination available stock; same world-time order: arrival verification before reservation, production, consumption; duplicate arrival ids rejected; in-transit stock is neither consumed nor double-counted",
      "source": "economy-owner.20261003.arrival; scope-map /decisions/23"
    },
    {
      "id": "peace-signing-gates",
      "statement": "Unregistered price versions lock signing and settlement; no duplicate demand of one ledger asset; V<=W is not automatic acceptance. Lock closure input, recheck continuing CB validity and eligible beneficiary first; an already invalid CB follows invalidation instead of generating rights even at W=100. With a valid CB, reaching +/-100 before acceptance closes under that CB version first and discards unaccepted proposals. Rights go to eligible beneficiary, not commander/approver by role. Same-boundary acceptance/100/death use established event order/version for a single settlement. Signed items remain campaign delivery/performance obligations, not inventory copies.",
      "source": "sp1.b34, sp1.b119, sp1.b121, sp1.b124-b127, sp1.reference.beneficiary"
    },
    {
      "id": "marriage-property-boundary",
      "statement": "marriage applies country institutions and records effects; formation alone grants no new claim or territory; on death/detention/office-loss each property effect is separately kept, ended, or re-ratified; a marriage record is not a will",
      "source": "claims-owner.20261003.marriage; scope-map /decisions/25"
    },
    {
      "id": "persons-not-transferable",
      "statement": "persons and recognized synthetic persons are not transferable assets; person demands are valid acts (release, repatriation, meeting, voluntary assignment)",
      "source": "sp1.b122, sp1.b61"
    },
    {
      "id": "custody-owner-role-independence",
