## Basis and Adoption Boundary

The only references to the original work are the GURPS Fourth Edition preview that was read directly and edition-specific comparisons with each preserved document. The Seoul approval boundary is maintained only up to that boundary. The owner''s choice is a selected partial policy, not a full contract or implementation certification. Data types and the additional current-custodian check are unadopted proposals. Missing figures, systems, and original rules remain undecided.

## Situation Report Deliverables

[Situation Report](https://evidence.linalab.io/evidence/seoul-gdd-sheets-situations-20261007-f2bbda37-c30b-4c23-8684-b51724045d48/situations.html) · [Domain Design Proposal Reader](https://evidence.linalab.io/evidence/seoul-gdd-sheets-situations-20261007-f2bbda37-c30b-4c23-8684-b51724045d48/index.html). The reader is a design document that distinguishes the approved scope from unadopted proposals. The situations for each domain can be read in [Domain Situations and Cases](/gdd/system-design/domain-situations/).

